Reason: collision events took their turns object by object in the order of the lowest object each one collides with,
so Samus's beam (oBeam, whose first target is oBlockShoot) went long before AM2R's door (oDoor). Every door builds a
solid block beside itself, and a power beam that reaches the door touches that block in the same frame: its oSolid
event destroyed it before the door's oBeam event could open the door, so blue doors only opened to missiles (issue
#1). The native runner takes the turns in object index order, which puts the door first; the list is now built in
that order once, at load.
Upstream: Bug on every platform - upstream fixed it on 2026-10-31 (ea5e8c2, "fix(collision): sort events in ascending
order", which sorts a copy every frame). Retires this patch when the pin moves past it.

--- a/src/runner.c
+++ b/src/runner.c
@@ -3101,6 +3101,13 @@
                 arrput(runner->objectsWithAnyEventOfType[t], obj);
             }
         }
+
+        // The native runner takes collision turns in object index order: AM2R's door must catch a beam before the
+        // beam's own solid event destroys it on the door's block.
+        if (t == EVENT_COLLISION) {
+            arrsetlen(runner->objectsWithAnyEventOfType[t], 0);
+            repeat(objectCount, obj) if (seen[obj]) arrput(runner->objectsWithAnyEventOfType[t], obj);
+        }
     }
 
     free(seen);
